Upstream: and-gue/NeaTS@2d804ff492e45222e841dc1a50904476fa64f4a0

LeaTS declares a complete in-memory codec but its serialize/load block is commented
and was copied from NeaTS with fields that LeaTS does not own. This patch enables the
block after removing those invalid NeaTS-only fields. It serializes every LeaTS field
needed by scalar full decode and operator[]: max_bpc, logical length, residual bit
count, both Elias-Fano structures, packed residuals, bits-per-correction, and the two
linear coefficients arrays.

The patch also selects the scalar tail loop in residual construction. This avoids an
unsupported GCC 11 experimental-simd conversion without changing the stored values.
